WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:05.259
Hey YouTubers, it's Charlie. So Agents
of S.H.I.E.L.D. is back tonight so I thought I'd do

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:09.460
a refresher video on the Inhumans. The back 
half of Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. Season 2

00:00:09.469 --> 00:00:13.139
is gonna be all about explaining who
their culture, their society are.

00:00:13.139 --> 00:00:17.279
The Inhumans that you see in the Marvel
Cinematic Universe, in the TV shows, in the movies,

00:00:17.289 --> 00:00:20.470
are gonna be a little bit different from
what they are in the comics so I'll try to

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:21.840
explain what the difference is.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.360
But I'm gonna start with their original
origin story from the comics. They suffer

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:28.200
from the same problem that a lot of big
Marvel characters have.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.099
They belong to a group of people whose
origin is tied to

00:00:32.099 --> 00:00:35.370
another group that Marvel no longer has
the IP for, for

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:40.140
the films and TV shows. So let's get
started. The characters were created by Stan Lee

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:44.900
and Jack Kirby, so totally expect a
Stan Lee cameo in 2019, whenever the movie comes.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:48.720
They appeared for the first time in Fantastic Four #45.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:52.020
In that issue Stan Lee introed most of who
would become

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:56.239
the Royal Family, but at the time the
Inhumans were just these few characters.

00:00:56.239 --> 00:01:00.110
There was Black Bolt, Crystal, Medusa,

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:03.230
Gorgon, Karnak, Lockjaw

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:07.780
and Triton. The plot of some of those early
Stan Lee stories was kinda whimsical but

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:11.440
it was the swinging sixties, which I know
sounds kinda like a Spider-Man joke, but

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.900
you get the idea. You know, the characters 
were really interesting

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:17.510
but sometimes some of the story beats
were a little bit funny.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:21.380
So the first time we see them Johnny
Storm is getting stood up for a date

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:24.500
and as he's grumbling his way walking
back to the Baxter Building

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:28.580
he sees a mysterious redhead in an
alleyway who turns out to be Crystal.

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:32.369
Mystified, he tries to follow her, shows
her his powers in an alleyway

00:01:32.369 --> 00:01:36.130
which isn't a euphemism for pulling his
pants down. If he did that today he would

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:37.360
totally get arrested.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:41.000
"Let's go to this dark alleyway and I'll
show you something really special."

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:46.240
Crystal reveals that she also has
special powers, introduces her special dog, Lockjaw,

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:49.530
he opens a portal and Crystal takes
Johnny Storm to her home.

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:53.200
Nowadays this would be a story that
parents would show their kids to tell them

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:57.070
why you don't go home with strangers. So
Johnny Storm gets to see

00:01:57.070 --> 00:02:01.509
Attilan for the first time, that's the
Inhuman's secret city that's cloaked from view.

00:02:01.509 --> 00:02:04.670
Across their history in the comics
it's moved around in terms of its

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:06.460
location relative to Earth but

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:09.539
initially it started on the Moon. Here's
where things get a little bit funny.

00:02:09.539 --> 00:02:13.270
Johnny Storm meets the rest of the Royal
Family and realizes that he's seen

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:17.900
Medusa as part of the Frightful Four, they're like an
evil version of the Fantastic Four.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:21.819
So remember, this is issue number 45 when
we're seeing them for the first time.

00:02:21.819 --> 00:02:26.989
Medusa appeared in issue number 36 in an
evil team up called the Frightful Four.

00:02:26.989 --> 00:02:31.629
I think what probably ended up happening
is Stan Lee liked her character so much

00:02:31.629 --> 00:02:35.489
that he wanted to make her an Inhuman but
had to find a way to explain how she

00:02:35.489 --> 00:02:36.670
could be in that team

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:40.359
and also be an Inhuman. So the official
explanation became that

00:02:40.359 --> 00:02:43.810
she had amnesia quote-unquote while she was
fighting with

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:47.290
the Frightful Four. Stan Lee has a long
history a moving characters around in

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:50.370
terms of, you know, what their stories
are, which teams they belong to.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:54.170
Sometimes it creates some continuity errors.
Nowadays what Marvel does

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:57.340
is they just create, like,
earth-shattering universe events like

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:59.019
the Battle World stuff that's happening.

00:02:59.019 --> 00:03:02.269
So after that first appearance, the
Inhumans just kinda bounced around a

00:03:02.269 --> 00:03:03.359
couple different titles

00:03:03.359 --> 00:03:07.349
until they get their own title in 1975.
It only ran for about twelve issues.

00:03:07.349 --> 00:03:10.209
That trend continued for a little while.
They would just get limited runs from

00:03:10.209 --> 00:03:12.859
time to time. So they got another one in 1998,

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:16.220
then a different one in 2000,
then again in 2003

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:20.720
and 2007. So as you can see they've been
kind of like this weird little group of

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:23.129
characters that Marvel brings out every
once in a while

00:03:23.129 --> 00:03:26.799
but historically they were never popular
enough to sustain their own ongoing

00:03:26.799 --> 00:03:28.730
title like the bigger Marvel characters.

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:31.940
That might change whenever the movie
comes out though. Movie sales always

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:33.730
boost Marvel's comic sales.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:37.590
After that first Robert Downey Jr.
Iron Man came out, sales of Iron Man comics

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:40.849
shot through the roof. The lore of
Inhumans is really cool too

00:03:40.849 --> 00:03:44.120
but like a lot of Stan Lee characters
he introduces the characters first

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:47.709
and then, like, many issues later he'll
flesh out their backstory.

00:03:47.709 --> 00:03:51.359
Originally their backstory was tied to
the Kree-Skrull war.

00:03:51.359 --> 00:03:54.709
The Kree were looking for a weapon to
use against the Skrull so they spent

00:03:54.709 --> 00:03:59.329
millennia genetically tampering with humans on Earth. Eventually they abandoned the project

00:03:59.329 --> 00:04:02.690
after a prophecy predicted that an
Inhuman would rise and destroy the

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:03.819
Supreme Intelligence

00:04:03.819 --> 00:04:07.359
who failed to appear in the Guardains of the Galaxy movie. I know we're all hoping to see

00:04:07.359 --> 00:04:11.629
more Kree in Guardians of the Galaxy Two but
it's not confirmed. So while all this Kree-Skrull

00:04:11.629 --> 00:04:14.239
war stuff was going on the Inhumans overtime

00:04:14.239 --> 00:04:17.829
developed their own internal society. The
biggest part of their culture

00:04:17.829 --> 00:04:21.320
was based on genetic engineering in this
rigid caste structure.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.389
It dictated what jobs you could have,

00:04:23.389 --> 00:04:28.860
who you could marry, so naturally by design the most powerful Inhumans were members of the Royal Family

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:32.250
and they are very xenophobic which is
why even after the Kree abandoned them they

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:34.130
continued to keep their city hidden.

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:37.880
Black Bolt is a member the Illuminati and
appears in the Avengers a lot but

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:42.580
Crystal has historically been their
biggest ambassador in terms of crossover characters.

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:46.900
She's been a member of Fantastic Four
and she was a member of the Avengers for a long time,

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:51.380
Medusa to a lesser extent too. There was, like, a
very Romeo and Juliet thing going on

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:54.690
with Johnny Storm and Crystal for a
long time so that was like a way

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:56.599
to bridge their cultures in the comics.

00:04:56.599 --> 00:05:01.119
For the most part they are allies with
the heroes of Earth but they still have their own agenda

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:04.930
I mean it's like Namor and Black Panther,
they both serve with the Illuminati

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:09.500
but their first priority is always to
their own people. So let's move into Terrigenesis,

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:14.780
that is the foundation for their society
and the process by which they activate their powers.

00:05:14.789 --> 00:05:18.949
So taking in the Mists and getting powers
isn't what makes someone an Inhuman,

00:05:18.949 --> 00:05:22.030
that's something that's passed down
through genetics. So there are

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:26.430
Inhumans walking around that have not
taken in the Mist, that don't have special powers.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:29.780
But in order to take advantage of the
Mist you do have to have those

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:33.159
Inhuman genetic markers. The TV show
kind of explored this

00:05:33.159 --> 00:05:37.319
where, like, Skye, Trip, and Raina all took
in the Mist but Trip did not have

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:39.320
Inhuman DNA so it killed him

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:44.219
and gave powers to Skye and Raina. The TV
show's really simplified the process by which

00:05:44.219 --> 00:05:48.190
Terrigenesis happens, you know, and how
they find these other Inhuman people.

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:51.169
They've kind of tied it to the Kree but I
don't know how much they're gonna

00:05:51.169 --> 00:05:52.169
explain that because

00:05:52.169 --> 00:05:55.710
the Kree are largely a group that show up
in the Guardians of the Galaxy movies

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:59.009
so they might keep them there. Most of
what we see on the TV show

00:05:59.009 --> 00:06:02.949
is just gonna focus on the Inhumans
living on Earth in secret groups.

00:06:02.949 --> 00:06:06.300
So I'm not expecting to see Attilan or any
of the Royal Family.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:09.969
What I'm hoping is is that they weave
the idea of the Inhumans living on Earth

00:06:09.969 --> 00:06:11.930
into Age of Ultron, Civil War,

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:15.880
and the rest the movies, obviously
building up to the actual Inhumans movie.

